Description: Rust programming language toolchain (official stable release)
 The official Rust stable toolchain as published by the Rust project:
 rustc, cargo, rustdoc, rustfmt, clippy and rust-analyzer, plus the
 standard library for the host. The binaries are exactly the ones rustup
 installs, verified against the Rust release signing key, and updated with
 every stable release.
 .
 The toolchain lives in /usr/lib/rust-stable with its own bundled LLVM, and
 the commands are linked into /usr/bin. It replaces the distribution's
 rustc, cargo, rustfmt, rust-clippy, rust-analyzer and rustup packages
 (apt lists what it removes and asks first) and leaves the system LLVM and
 Ubuntu's versioned rustc-1.XX packages untouched.
 .
 This is an unofficial package.

Package: rust-stable-src
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: rust-stable (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Rust programming language toolchain (standard library source)
 Source code of the Rust standard library for the rust-stable toolchain,
 in its sysroot (what rustup calls the rust-src component). rust-analyzer
 needs it for completion and go-to-definition into std.
 .
 This is an unofficial package.

Package: rust-stable-doc
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Section: doc
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Enhances: rust-stable
Description: Rust programming language toolchain (offline documentation)
 The offline HTML documentation shipped with each Rust release: the
 standard library API, The Rust Programming Language book, Rust by
 Example, the Cargo book, the reference, the edition guide and more,
 under /usr/share/doc/rust-stable-doc/html.
 .
 This is an unofficial package.

Package: rust-stable-std-musl
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: rust-stable (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Rust programming language toolchain (musl target)
 The Rust standard library for the host's musl target
 (x86_64-unknown-linux-musl on amd64, aarch64-unknown-linux-musl on
 arm64), for building fully static Linux binaries with
 cargo build --target <triple>. It brings its own musl C library, so no
 musl-tools package is needed.
 .
 This is an unofficial package.

Package: rust-stable-std-wasm32-unknown-unknown
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: rust-stable (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Rust programming language toolchain (wasm32-unknown-unknown target)
 The Rust standard library for the wasm32-unknown-unknown target, used for
 WebAssembly in the browser (wasm-bindgen, wasm-pack, Trunk, Leptos,
 Yew). Linking uses the rust-lld that ships with rust-stable.
 .
 This is an unofficial package.

Package: rust-stable-std-wasm32-wasip1
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: rust-stable (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Rust programming language toolchain (wasm32-wasip1 target)
 The Rust standard library for the wasm32-wasip1 target (WASI preview 1),
 for WebAssembly programs that run under wasmtime, wasmer and other WASI
 runtimes.
 .
 This is an unofficial package.

Package: rust-stable-std-wasm32-wasip2
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: rust-stable (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Rust programming language toolchain (wasm32-wasip2 target)
 The Rust standard library for the wasm32-wasip2 target (WASI preview 2,
 the component model). Components are produced with the wasm-component-ld
 that ships with rust-stable.
 .
 This is an unofficial package.
